      "text": "To evaluate the expression \\(\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\cdots}}}}\\), we start by letting \\( x \\) represent the entire expression. This gives us the equation:\n\n\\[\nx = \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\cdots}}}}\n\\]\n\nSince the expression inside the square root is the same as the entire expression, we can rewrite the equation as:\n\n\\[\nx = \\sqrt{2 - x}\n\\]\n\nNext, we square both sides of the equation to eliminate the square root:\n\n\\[\nx^2 = 2 - x\n\\]\n\nRearrange the equation to form a standard quadratic equation:\n\n\\[\nx^2 + x - 2 = 0\n\\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 1 \\), and \\( c = -2 \\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-2)}}{2 \\cdot 1}\n\\]\n\nSimplify inside the square root:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 8}}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{9}}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-1 \\pm 3}{2}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two potential solutions:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-1 + 3}{2} = \\frac{2}{2} = 1\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-1 - 3}{2} = \\frac{-4}{2} = -2\n\\]\n\nSince \\( x \\) represents a nested square root expression, it must be non-negative. Therefore, we discard the negative solution \\( x = -2 \\) and keep:\n\n\\[\nx = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the expression \\(\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2 - \\cdots}}}}\\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
